$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Compound 10: A mixture of 11 (0.20 g, 0.78 mmol), EDCI (0.18 g, 0.78
mmol), and DMAP (0.19 g, 1.55 mmol) in anhydrous DMF was stirred under
nitrogen for 10 min at room temperature. Dopamine hydrochloride (0.15 g,
0.78 mmol) was then added to the mixture. The reaction mixture was
stirred overnight. The solvent was evaporated off, after which CH2Cl2 (50
mL) and water (50 mL) were added, and the organic layer was collected.
The CH2Cl2 layer was dried with anhydrous MgSO4. After removal of the
solvents, the crude product was purified over silica gel using
CH2Cl2/MeOH (v/v, 97:3) as the eluent. 10 as a yellowish solid (0.22 g,
72%). 1H-NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 8.92 (s, 1H), 8.67 (s, 1H), 7.42 (d, J =
9.02 Hz, 1H), 6.84-6.80 (m, 2H), 6.69-6.63 (m, 2H), 6.48 (s, 1H), 5.64
(s, 2H), 3.68-3.61 (q, J = 8.46 Hz, 2H), 3.49-3.42 (q, J = 8.88 Hz, 4H),
2.83-2.78 (t, J = 8.04 Hz, 2H), 1.26-1.22 (t, J = 7.54 Hz, 6H). 13C-NMR
(100 MHz, DMSO-d 6): 162.1, 161.7, 157.2, 152.4, 147.7, 145.1, 143.6,
131.6, 130.0, 119.3, 116.0, 115.6, 110.1, 109.4, 107.7, 95.9, 44.4, 40.8,
34.6, 12.3. ESI-MS calc. for C22H24N2O5 [M+H]+ 397.17, found 397.30.
