$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Salicylic acid (1.8 mmol), thionyl chloride
(3.6 mmol), a drop of DMF were dissolved in dichloromethane (15 mL) and
the mixture was heated to reflux for 3 hours. The resulting solution was
poured into an ice bath, sat. aq. NaHCO3 (12 mL) was added and stirred
for 1 minute. Subsequently crude 2-amino-2-naphthophenone was added and
the solution was warmed up to room temperature. After 2 hours, the
solution was extracted with dichloromethane (4* 20 mL ) and sat. aq. NaCl
(20 mL), The organic layer was dried over Na2SO4, then purified by flash
chromatography on silica gel with ethyl acetate and petroleum ether. The
product 3d. Yellow solid; eluent: petroleum ether/ethyl acetate (5:1).
2-Hydroxy-5-methoxy-N-(2-oxo-2-phenyl-ethyl)-benzamide (3i). Yield: 114
mg (70%), pale yellow solid; eluent: petroleum ether/ethyl acetate (4:1).
Mp.: 177.0-178.0 °C. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 11.62 (s, 1H), 8.04 (dd, J
= 8.3, 1.2 Hz, 2H), 7.69-7.64 (m, 1H), 7.54 (dd, J = 10.8, 4.7 Hz, 2H),
7.46 (bs, 1H), 7.07-7.04 (m, 2H), 6.96 (t, J = 1.4 Hz, 1H), 4.93 (d, J =
4.1 Hz, 2H), 3.83 (s, 3H); 13C NMR (101 MHz, CDCl3) δ 193.7, 169.7,
155.7, 151.9, 134.5, 134.1, 129.1, 128.0, 121.6, 119.3, 113.7, 109.8,
56.1, 46.4; IR (neat): 3424, 1686, 1577, 1447, 1365, 1218, 1000, 832,
768, 755, 688, 630 (cm-1); HRMS (ESI/TOF) m/z calcd. for C16H15NO4
[M+Na]+: 308.08933, found: 308.08962.
